          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: le plâtre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le plâtre — \"plaster cast; plaster\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mon fils a eu la jambe dans le plâtre pendant six semaines. My son had his leg in a cast for six weeks."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Être dans le plâtre — to be in a cast. Also building plaster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le plâtre comes from Old French plastre, which goes back to Latin emplastrum \"a plaster for a wound\", a borrowing from Greek émplastron."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
